# Player controls are frozen

The **player controls** and the player screens confirmed on devices are **approved as-is**. Do **not** modify them unless the user **explicitly countermands** this rule (for example “change the player controls”, “lift the player freeze”, “move the decimal”).

This covers `apps/player` and any shared code whose change would alter what a player sees or taps. Host, server, and public-display work stays allowed when the player picture stays the same.

## Approved screens

Join, connecting, waiting room, the pre-deal table, the question, your turn, your guess, guess sent, folded, results, the next question, and game over. Hold to peek and the in-hand Quit stay as they are.

## Do not change (without explicit user request)

- Where a control sits, its label, its size, or which controls a screen has
- The wide oval, the question box, the bet buttons, or the call line
- The guess keypad, the decimal beside the hole cards, or the street cards on one row
- Seat names, chip amounts, results columns, or the pre-deal table
- Spacing, type size, or “drive-by” refactors that move these styles and alter how a control looks

The responsive and surgical player rules still describe the bar those screens already meet. They do not authorize another pass over a screen that already passed.

## Allowed without countermand

- Read-only investigation and answers about how a player screen works
- A crash or wrong-data fix that leaves the picture identical; say so in the commit message

## When the user countermands

Proceed with their specific instruction only for that turn (or the scope they name). Do not broaden it.

## Checklist before editing the player

- [ ] Would this change what a player sees or taps? If yes, did the user explicitly request it?
- [ ] If a player control was touched without that request, revert those hunks.
